            <ArticleTitle>Modifiers of exercise-induced S-T segment changes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>349-54</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myocardial ischemia due to coronary atherosclerosis is the usual cause of exercise-induced S-T segment changes. A number of drugs, electrolyte alterations, and hemodynamic factors may accentuate or mask these changes. The clinician should keep this in mind during the electrocardiographic interpretation of exercise tests.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
